@prefix surface: <sem://surface#> .
@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/> .
@prefix graphql: <https://pragma.canonical.com/graphql#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .


# The surface ontology: the demand model a documentation site is specified
# against. Jobs say what consumers are trying to get done, coordinates say
# who has them, pairings reify which surface serves which job and at what
# reorientation cost, and slots tie the design system's layouts to the jobs
# that summon their regions.
#
# Every class and property is described by its rdfs:comment, which the
# GraphQL compiler copies verbatim into the schema as the type's or field's
# description; edit a comment and the docs site's committed schema changes.
# Cardinalities live in shapes.ttl, never in owl:FunctionalProperty, because
# the compiler reads singular and list fields from the SHACL shapes.

surface: a owl:Ontology ;
  rdfs:label "Surface Ontology" ;
  rdfs:comment "The demand model of a documentation site: jobs, the coordinates of who has them, the surfaces that serve them, the pairings between the two, and the layout slots each job summons." .

surface:Validity a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Validity" ;
  rdfs:comment "Why an item is no longer (or never was) live: superseded, deprecated, cancelled or rejected (data/validities.ttl). Invalid items STAY in the graph with a note — the know-your-neighbour rule: anyone who finds the node learns its fate and its reason. Distinct from deferred (still wanted, consciously parked) and from assume:status (the epistemics of assumptions). Absence of validity means live." .

surface:Verdict a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Verdict" ;
  rdfs:comment "The result of walking an exemplar: renders (completes cleanly), ceremony (completes but awkwardly — a friction worth recording) or wall (cannot complete — a real gap). Instances in data/verdicts.ttl. A verdict is dated and cites the surfaces walked; re-walking on a spec change is the regression test." .

surface:Exemplar a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Exemplar" ;
  rdfs:comment "A worked story walked against the specification to a verdict — the sufficiency test that jobs (existence) and bets (assumption) cannot give. Where the no-job-no-element law grounds why a surface exists, an exemplar grounds whether the surfaces a job touches actually let a real person complete it. A story that cannot complete across a job's served surfaces is a wall found before anything is built; one that completes only awkwardly is a ceremony; one that completes cleanly renders." .

surface:Law a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Law" ;
  rdfs:comment "A named, reusable discipline of well-specified surfaces — the distilled cross-corpus rules (one substrate many projections; every word has one home; four states or it doesn't ship). Laws are cited by grammars (grammar:law) and instantiated by project rulings (assume:derivedFrom). A sibling of Axiom and Heuristic under assume:Assumption, deliberately outside their id/phase regimes: laws are timeless, not scheduled." .

surface:Bet a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Bet" ;
  rdfs:comment "A falsifiable design assumption with a named test or kill-criterion — the third species of assumption beside the hard axiom and the soft heuristic. A bet without a kill-criterion is an opinion. Bets live in one shared ledger; jobs reference them by id; ids are stable and never renumbered (gaps mean retired bets). Modal character: P? — wagered, awaiting evidence." .

surface:Slot a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Slot" ;
  rdfs:comment "A layout's declaration of a region: which region, whether required, and — if optional — WHICH JOB SUMMONS IT: no job, no region. One canvas always; everything else earns its slot. Layouts themselves are ds:Layout instances, reused directly, carrying ds:grid and ds:name; surface adds the slot-and-demand layer ds lacks." .

surface:Region a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Region" ;
  rdfs:comment "A typed slot kind, one shared vocabulary so 'where is it' means the same thing on every surface. Base instances in data/regions.ttl: canvas, rails, controls, status and aside; a project's graph may add its own. A region type never changes side — the compass is part of the stationary frame." .

surface:Pairing a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Pairing" ;
  rdfs:comment "The reified job↔surface edge: THIS job reaches THIS surface, as primary or secondary, arriving with THIS preservation (curated surfaces only — ports take no arrival). The set of a job's pairings is how the spec answers 'is this job served, and at what cost'." .

surface:PairingRole a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Pairing role" ;
  rdfs:comment "Whether a pairing is the job's primary serving surface or a secondary route. Instances in data/arrivals.ttl: primary and secondary." .

surface:Preservation a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Preservation" ;
  rdfs:comment "What an arrival keeps, ordered by reorientation cost (reorientationOrder): cold_entry (4) keeps nothing; subject_kept (3) keeps the subject; view_kept (2) keeps view and subject; no_move (1) is in-place reach. Pure edge vocabulary: whether a surface can be called is a fact about the surface, never about an arrival. Instances in data/arrivals.ttl." .

surface:Port a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:label "Port" ;
  rdfs:comment "The invocable surface: where machine consumers call instead of look — API, MCP, CLI. Exposes capabilities directly; it curates nothing, so it has no slice, and pairings to it carry no arrival (agents have no reorientation to preserve)." .

surface:Editor a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:label "Editor" ;
  rdfs:comment "A standalone writing surface you dwell in: authoring against the substrate at large rather than at one subject." .

surface:ComposerSurface a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:label "Composer surface" ;
  rdfs:comment "An anchored writing surface: where a consumer puts value INTO the substrate at a subject — the run's composer, a proposal form on an entity. The write quadrant the kind-enum scheme could not express." .

surface:Mechanism a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:label "Mechanism" ;
  rdfs:comment "A View woven through everything: inline mentions, status glyphs. Its pairings arrive at no_move — reaching it costs nothing, which is its entire point." .

surface:Peek a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:label "Peek" ;
  rdfs:comment "A View you pass through: preview without commitment, one step back up. Its pairings typically arrive at subject_kept." .

surface:Detail a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:label "Detail" ;
  rdfs:comment "A View you dwell in: one entity in depth — the entity page, the spec sheet. Its pairings typically arrive at cold_entry (deep links) or subject_kept." .

surface:View a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:label "View" ;
  rdfs:comment "An anchored reading surface — curated, read-facing, subject-bound: it shows something OF something. Whether it is ambient (chips), transient (a peek), or dwelt-in (a detail page) is not a node fact: it shows in its pairings' arrivals." .

surface:Lens a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:subClassOf surface:Surface ;
  # Bound to another type name because the compiler mints both the singular
  # lookup and the plural listing root fields from the class name, and the
  # plural of "lens" is "lens": the two fields collide on Query.lens, which
  # the compiler treats as fatal (W001). "LensSurface" mints lensSurface and
  # lensSurfaces, the same pattern as ComposerSurface.
  graphql:name "LensSurface" ;
  rdfs:label "Lens" ;
  rdfs:comment "A way of looking at the substrate, tuned for one kind of task: curated, read-facing, standalone. You don't navigate into a lens like a folder — you switch lenses and the same entities re-present. A lens without a slice is a folder." .

surface:Anchoring a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Anchoring" ;
  rdfs:comment "Whether the surface is coherent standalone (Free) or meaningless without a subject (SubjectBound — a peek OF something)." .

surface:Direction a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Direction" ;
  rdfs:comment "Which way value flows at this surface: ReadFace (consumer takes) or WriteFace (consumer puts). Multi-valued — a surface may carry both." .

surface:Rendering a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Rendering" ;
  rdfs:comment "What the surface does with the substrate: curated (re-presents a chosen slice for perception) or invocable (exposes operations for calling). Instances in data/dimensions.ttl." .

surface:AuthorityFamily a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Authority family" ;
  rdfs:comment "The species of authority a capability requires. Base instances (data/authority-families.ttl): read, observe, write, control, genesis. A project's graph may add its own families. Reachability and authorization are two layers: authority flows through handles, but write-authorization is checked at the target regardless of which handle called." .

surface:Capability a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Capability" ;
  rdfs:comment "A named, grantable operation over the substrate — the unit of 'what the system can do'. Verbs in a grammar name capabilities; projections bind them; channels expose them to machine consumers. Object-capability shaped: authority flows through whoever hands you the handle; bundles compose capabilities; attenuation only narrows (the derived capability's authority is a subset of its parent's)." .

surface:Substrate a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Substrate" ;
  rdfs:comment "The single source of truth a surface projects: a knowledge graph, a journal, a store. One substrate, many projections — every view shows its own slice, no view shows all of it, and state is derived from the substrate, never duplicated beside it. If two surfaces disagree, the substrate arbitrates." .

surface:Persona a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Persona" ;
  rdfs:comment "A named region in coordinate space — an archetype used for coverage planning and QA, never for navigation. A persona's jobs are DERIVED by overlap of its region with each job's coordinates; asserting the persona↔job link directly is a modelling error (the link is derived, not stored)." .

surface:Fluency a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Fluency" ;
  rdfs:comment "Ordinal familiarity with the system on a coordinate axis: newcomer < fluent < expert (data/fluencies.ttl, ordered by fluencyOrder). Expert is a fluency waypoint, not a role — authority positions are roles." .

surface:Role a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Role" ;
  rdfs:comment "A consumer's discipline or authority position on a coordinate axis (engineer, designer, writer; author, operator). Authority is a role, not a fluency level. Project vocabulary: no base instances ship — each spec graph defines its own. An axis left unconstrained matches any role (wildcard)." .

surface:Actor a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Actor" ;
  rdfs:comment "The species of consumer on a coordinate axis. Base instances: human and agent (data/actors.ttl). Surfaces are bi-modal by default — a machine consumer is a first-class actor, not an afterthought." .

surface:Coordinate a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Coordinate" ;
  rdfs:comment "A reified position or region in demand space, on three axes: actor, role and fluency. An axis left unconstrained matches any value. Reified so that jobs and personas share ONE type: a job's coordinates and a persona's region are compared axis by axis, and the persona↔job link is derived by overlap, never stored." .

surface:Job a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Job" ;
  rdfs:comment "The unit of demand and of value (jobs-to-be-done). One thing a consumer is trying to get done, written as a story: when [circumstance], I want [desire], so I can [outcome], without [pain]. Jobs — not personas, not features — drive surface requirements: every surface element must trace back to at least one job; a job with no serving surface is a coverage gap, and a surface element with no job is decoration." .

surface:Surface a owl:Class ;
  rdfs:label "Surface" ;
  rdfs:comment "An addressable place of encounter between a consumer and the substrate. Its nature is carried by three dimensions (rendering, direction, anchoring); the idiom classes below are named cells whose dimension values materialize through the closure — assert the idiom, infer the physics. A surface matching no idiom is asserted as a plain Surface with raw dimensions: fully described, honestly unnamed. How a surface is PRESENT (ambient, transient, dwelt-in) is edge information and lives on pairings as arrival — never on the node." .

surface:homedIn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:range surface:Lens ;
  rdfs:label "homed in" ;
  rdfs:comment "The lens where a noun's mentions land, and where a chip's jump goes: the noun's canonical home. Its domain is open by design: nouns pair with their home in data. The object form of grammar:home's prose — shapeable: the one-home law becomes checkable data, and a noun without a homedIn target is a visible work item, not a mystery." .

surface:supersededBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:label "superseded by" ;
  rdfs:comment "The successor item. Required when validity is superseded — a supersession without a forwarding address strands the neighbours." .

surface:validity a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:range surface:Validity ;
  rdfs:label "validity" ;
  rdfs:comment "This item's invalidity, when it has one. Explained by one validityNote; superseded requires supersededBy. Never delete — tombstone." .

surface:rendersIn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:range surface:Slot ;
  rdfs:label "renders in" ;
  rdfs:comment "What fills a slot — a surface now, components later (domain deliberately open). Where a surface has rendersIn, its within is DERIVABLE (slot → layout → composing surface) and an asserted within must agree; within remains the layout-free shorthand for specs that skip layouts." .

surface:declaresSlot a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:range surface:Slot ;
  rdfs:label "declares slot" ;
  rdfs:comment "A typed slot this layout declares. Domain deliberately open (the subject is a ds:Layout instance)." .

surface:composes a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:range ds:Layout ;
  rdfs:label "composes" ;
  rdfs:comment "A curated surface composes a layout — its division of space. Domain deliberately open (lenses and views both compose). Range is ds:Layout DIRECTLY: the design system owns layouts; this model attaches demand to them." .

surface:expandsTo a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:range surface:Region ;
  rdfs:label "expands to" ;
  rdfs:comment "An embedded curated surface can expand out of its host slot into a larger region — the folded-to-fullscreen affordance. A graph shown folded below the fold on an entity page expands into the overlay; a rail can expand into the canvas. The expansion is a presentation state, not a second surface: same slice, more room. When present, the surface owes a stated collapsed floor (it must be usable BEFORE expansion) — expansion is enhancement, never the only working size." .

surface:granted a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:range surface:Capability ;
  rdfs:label "granted" ;
  rdfs:comment "The capability (usually a bundle) this holder actually receives — the grant record. Grants make authority auditable: the parity query compares what agent and human holders reach; narrowing applies through attenuates chains, never by widening." .

surface:serves a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:range surface:Job ;
  rdfs:label "serves" ;
  rdfs:comment "The universal traceability edge: links a capability, surface, or component to a job it serves. Domain deliberately open. Operational grounding in one property — an element with no serves edge (direct or via its pairings) has no reason to exist." .

surface:over a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:range surface:Substrate ;
  rdfs:label "over" ;
  rdfs:comment "Links a capability (and later a lens) to the substrate it operates over or projects. Domain deliberately open: both capabilities and lenses use it." .

surface:validityNote a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "validity note" ;
  rdfs:comment "The mandatory comment on an invalid item: what happened, decided where, and what to use instead." .

surface:wakeCondition a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "wake condition" ;
  rdfs:comment "What must become true for this deferred item to wake — the written trigger that turns a parked promise into scheduled work. A deferral with a wake condition is a roadmap; without one it is furniture. Sources phrase these as 'when X exists / earns it / matures'; carry that language." .

surface:deferred a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
  rdfs:label "deferred" ;
  rdfs:comment "This job is explicitly parked by the spec (its status note carries the reason and trigger). Exempts it from the served gate (JobShape) — a job must be served or consciously deferred, never silently unserved." .

surface:verdict a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Exemplar ;
  rdfs:range surface:Verdict ;
  rdfs:label "verdict" ;
  rdfs:comment "How the walk came out: renders, ceremony or wall." .

surface:walksSurface a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Exemplar ;
  rdfs:range surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:label "walks surface" ;
  rdfs:comment "The surface(s) the story passes through — what a wall or ceremony verdict indicts, and what a spec change must re-walk." .

surface:walksJob a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Exemplar ;
  rdfs:range surface:Job ;
  rdfs:label "walks job" ;
  rdfs:comment "The job(s) this exemplar exercises — the demand it puts under load. Multi-valued: the strongest exemplars walk several jobs in one story." .

surface:finding a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Exemplar ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "finding" ;
  rdfs:comment "What the walk revealed — the wall's location, the ceremony's friction, or the clean-completion note. The reason the exemplar is kept." .

surface:narrative a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Exemplar ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "narrative" ;
  rdfs:comment "The story, walked step by step — what the person does, in order, against the named surfaces." .

surface:confidence a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Bet ;
  rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
  rdfs:label "confidence" ;
  rdfs:comment "The prior, 0..1 — how strongly the bet is believed before the instrument reports. A ledger you can be measurably wrong about builds judgment; scoring recorded confidence against outcomes is calibration. Distinct from assume:status (the epistemic state); this is the number." .

surface:instrument a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Bet ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "instrument" ;
  rdfs:comment "The concrete instrument that arms this bet — the thing that must exist and run to produce the evidence (a CI job, referrer analytics, a parity diff). A bet with a test but no instrument names a kill-criterion nobody is measuring; naming the instrument is what makes an armed bet continuously tested." .

surface:test a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Bet ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "test" ;
  rdfs:comment "The test or kill-criterion that would validate or kill this bet." .

surface:summonedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Slot ;
  rdfs:range surface:Job ;
  rdfs:label "summoned by" ;
  rdfs:comment "The job that summons this optional slot into existence. The load-bearing traceability rule of layout: no job → the region does not exist there. What keeps layout job-derived rather than template-derived." .

surface:ofRegion a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Slot ;
  rdfs:range surface:Region ;
  rdfs:label "of region" ;
  rdfs:comment "The region kind this slot instantiates." .

surface:required a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Slot ;
  rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
  rdfs:label "required" ;
  rdfs:comment "Always present (true) or optional (false). Optional slots MUST name their summoning job — the grid collapses over undemanded regions." .

surface:pairingRole a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Pairing ;
  rdfs:range surface:PairingRole ;
  rdfs:label "pairing role" ;
  rdfs:comment "primary or secondary." .

surface:arrival a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Pairing ;
  rdfs:range surface:Preservation ;
  rdfs:label "arrival" ;
  rdfs:comment "What this arrival preserves. Required for curated surfaces; absent for ports." .

surface:pairsSurface a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Pairing ;
  rdfs:range surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:label "pairs surface" ;
  rdfs:comment "The surface the job reaches." .

surface:forJob a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Pairing ;
  rdfs:range surface:Job ;
  rdfs:label "for job" ;
  rdfs:comment "The job this pairing serves." .

surface:reorientationOrder a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Preservation ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "reorientation order" ;
  rdfs:comment "Cost rank of the arrival, 4 (cold) to 1 (in place). Lets coverage ask: is a job whose story says 'without context-switching' really served at order 4?" .

surface:pairedIn a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:range surface:Pairing ;
  owl:inverseOf surface:pairsSurface ;
  rdfs:label "paired in" ;
  rdfs:comment "The pairings this surface participates in (inverse of pairsSurface) — materialized by the closure so surfaces connect outward without walking reification by hand." .

surface:within a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:range surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:label "within" ;
  rdfs:comment "Placement: this surface lives inside another (the composer within the canvas). Altitude is the derived length of the within-chain — never a stored number." .

surface:anchoring a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:range surface:Anchoring ;
  rdfs:label "anchoring" ;
  rdfs:comment "The surface's anchoring dimension. Usually inferred from the idiom class." .

surface:direction a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:range surface:Direction ;
  rdfs:label "direction" ;
  rdfs:comment "The surface's direction dimension(s). Usually inferred from the idiom class." .

surface:rendering a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Surface ;
  rdfs:range surface:Rendering ;
  rdfs:label "rendering" ;
  rdfs:comment "The surface's rendering dimension. Usually inferred from the idiom class; asserted directly only on unnamed hybrids." .

surface:exposes a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Port ;
  rdfs:range surface:Capability ;
  rdfs:label "exposes" ;
  rdfs:comment "What is callable at this port. Expose the passable units (bundles) rather than raw verbs — handles do the granting. A capability serving an agent-inclusive job but exposed on no port is unreachable by its own demand: the bi-modality gap, one query." .

surface:protocol a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Port ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "protocol" ;
  rdfs:comment "The protocol(s) this port speaks (MCP, GraphQL, CLI, a control socket)." .

surface:dominantJob a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Lens ;
  rdfs:range surface:Job ;
  rdfs:label "dominant job" ;
  rdfs:comment "The job that orders this lens's space — not role, not alphabet." .

surface:kindOfLooking a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Lens ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "kind of looking" ;
  rdfs:comment "The shape of looking this lens is tuned for — the clustering key that derived it from the jobs (entity browsing, narrative reading, live record…)." .

surface:slice a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Lens ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "slice" ;
  rdfs:comment "Which slice of the substrate this lens projects. No lens shows the whole substrate; a lens without a slice is a folder." .

surface:attenuates a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Capability ;
  rdfs:range surface:Capability ;
  rdfs:label "attenuates" ;
  rdfs:comment "This capability is a narrowing of another: same operations over less (fewer names, fewer targets), authority a subset of the parent's. Attenuation is the only sanctioned derivation of authority — it never widens." .

surface:bundles a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Capability ;
  rdfs:range surface:Capability ;
  rdfs:label "bundles" ;
  rdfs:comment "This capability is a thin bundle over the listed capabilities (a reader bundles read + snapshot + follow; a controller bundles deliver + lifecycle). Bundles exist to pass and attenuate scoped authority, never to add operations." .

surface:requiresAuthority a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Capability ;
  rdfs:range surface:AuthorityFamily ;
  rdfs:label "requires authority" ;
  rdfs:comment "The authority families this capability needs (multi-valued). Authority is explicit, never ambient." .

surface:contract a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Capability ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "contract" ;
  rdfs:comment "The capability's data contract: the query, signature, or verb form that every face of the surface binds. One contract, two faces — the human projection and the machine tool carry the same one, so they cannot drift." .

surface:fluencyOrder a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Fluency ;
  rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
  rdfs:label "fluency order" ;
  rdfs:comment "Ordinal position on the arc (1 = newcomer)." .

surface:region a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Persona ;
  rdfs:range surface:Coordinate ;
  rdfs:label "region" ;
  rdfs:comment "The coordinate region this persona names. Same type as a job's coordinates, so matching is axis-by-axis overlap." .

surface:essence a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Persona ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "essence" ;
  rdfs:comment "The persona in one line — what this archetype is about." .

surface:fluency a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Coordinate ;
  rdfs:range surface:Fluency ;
  rdfs:label "fluency" ;
  rdfs:comment "The fluency axis. Multi-valued (a region may span an arc); ABSENT MEANS ANY — wildcard, else intersection (same rule as role)." .

surface:role a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Coordinate ;
  rdfs:range surface:Role ;
  rdfs:label "role" ;
  rdfs:comment "The role axis of the coordinate. Multi-valued; ABSENT MEANS ANY ROLE — matching treats an unconstrained axis as a wildcard, otherwise requires intersection." .

surface:actor a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Coordinate ;
  rdfs:range surface:Actor ;
  rdfs:label "actor" ;
  rdfs:comment "The actor axis of the coordinate (human, agent). Multi-valued: a region may span both." .

surface:bet a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Job ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "bet" ;
  rdfs:comment "The assumptions this job's design leans on — typically Bets from the shared ledger. Shared across jobs: they live once, referenced by id." .

surface:coordinates a owl:ObjectProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Job ;
  rdfs:range surface:Coordinate ;
  rdfs:label "coordinates" ;
  rdfs:comment "Who has this job, as a coordinate region. The single source of truth for 'who'; persona columns in any table are derived views over this value." .

surface:acceptance a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Job ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "acceptance" ;
  rdfs:comment "A done-test clause for this job (multi-valued). The falsifiable answer to 'is this job served?' — a job without at least one acceptance clause is an opinion, not demand. Surfaces paired to the job inherit the clauses that mention them." .

surface:story a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
  rdfs:domain surface:Job ;
  rdfs:range xsd:string ;
  rdfs:label "story" ;
  rdfs:comment "The full job story in one sentence carrying the four slots: 'When [circumstance], I want [desire], so I can [outcome], without [pain]'. Kept as one string; reify the slots only when a real query needs slot-level joins." .
